IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `acc-types`
IMPORT `acc-cover`
IMPORT `acc-claims-disputes`
IMPORT `acc-entitlements`
IMPORT `acc-levies-offences`
IMPORT `acc-goal`

-- Independent tests: Accident Compensation Act 2001 (NZ).
-- Each assertion carries the E-number from independent-expectations.md.
-- The expected values were fixed from the source text before the encoding
-- was read, and have not been changed to match it.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVETH AN Occurrence
`a specific event` MEANS `(a) a specific event with an external force, a sudden avoiding movement, or a twist`

GIVEN occ IS AN Occurrence, h IS A Harm, c IS A Cause, d IS A DATE, nz IS A BOOLEAN, res IS A BOOLEAN, ship IS A BOOLEAN, conseq IS A BOOLEAN, cardio IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Injury facts`
injx MEANS `Injury facts` WITH
    `occurrence` IS occ
    `harm` IS h
    `cause` IS c
    `suffered on` IS d
    `in New Zealand` IS nz
    `ordinarily resident in New Zealand` IS res
    `on the ship or aircraft to, around or from New Zealand, or embarking` IS ship
    `consequence of treatment for a covered injury` IS conseq
    `a cardiovascular episode from abnormal work effort` IS cardio

GIVEN occ IS AN Occurrence, h IS A Harm, c IS A Cause, d IS A DATE, nz IS A BOOLEAN, res IS A BOOLEAN, ship IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Injury facts`
inj MEANS injx OF occ, h, c, d, nz, res, ship, FALSE, FALSE

-- an injury of a given harm and cause, in NZ, resident, 2010
GIVEN h IS A Harm, c IS A Cause
GIVETH AN `Injury facts`
pi MEANS inj OF `a specific event`, h, c, YMD 2010 6 1, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

GIVEN caused IS A BOOLEAN, ordinary IS A BOOLEAN, underlying IS A BOOLEAN, resource IS A BOOLEAN, consent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Treatment facts`
tf MEANS `Treatment facts` WITH
    `caused by treatment` IS caused
    `a necessary part or ordinary consequence of the treatment` IS ordinary
    `wholly or substantially caused by an underlying condition` IS underlying
    `solely a resource allocation decision` IS resource
    `unreasonably withheld or delayed consent` IS consent
    `the treatment was for a work-related injury` IS FALSE

GIVEN e4 IS A NUMBER, w4 IS A NUMBER, e52 IS A NUMBER, w52 IS A NUMBER, ft IS A BOOLEAN, minw IS A NUMBER, after IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Earnings facts`
ef MEANS `Earnings facts` WITH
    `earnings in the 4 weeks before incapacity` IS e4
    `weeks worked in those 4 weeks` IS w4
    `earnings in the 52 weeks before incapacity` IS e52
    `weeks worked in those 52 weeks` IS w52
    `in full-time employment or on the minimum levy` IS ft
    `minimum weekly earnings` IS minw
    `earnings after incapacity, per week` IS after

GIVEN sp IS A NUMBER, ch IS A NUMBER, od IS A NUMBER, both IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Survivor facts`
sf MEANS `Survivor facts` WITH
    `surviving spouses or partners` IS sp
    `children under 18` IS ch
    `other dependants` IS od
    `both parents of the child have died` IS both

GIVEN i IS AN `Injury facts`, t IS A `Treatment facts`, w IS A `Work circumstance`, v IS A `Vehicle involvement`, s IS AN `Earner status`, e IS AN `Earnings facts`, d IS A Disentitlement
GIVETH AN `Injury case`
case MEANS `Injury case` WITH
    `injury` IS i
    `treatment` IS t
    `work circumstance` IS w
    `vehicle` IS v
    `status` IS s
    `earnings` IS e
    `disentitlement` IS d

GIVETH A `Treatment facts`
`no treatment` MEANS tf OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- Fixture note: the minimum weekly earnings here is 500, below the $900
-- 52-week figure, so cl 42 does not lift it. (A first draft used 920, which
-- made the goal case below a cl 42 case; that was a fixture error, not a
-- change of expected value: E143's scenario has no minimum-earnings uplift.)
GIVETH AN `Earnings facts`
`standard earnings` MEANS ef OF 4000, 4, 46800, 52, TRUE, 500, 0

